items.description:
Drops every Lumi query when the tenant changes and fetches the mounted ones
again, as signing in does, so one tenant's cache never shows in another;
the live connection reopens with the new tenant.

members.description:
The app's request client at the panel's backend, signed by the auth provider the
Admin ends up with. `http.extend({ baseUrl })` reaches another backend;
`auth: false` sends no app credentials there.

fields.description:
`split` puts code and result side by side once the example is wide enough;
`stack` keeps the result below the code, for results that need the full
width, such as a table. Narrow examples always stack.

